<title>USA: U.N. sources see Iraq aid plan approved by weekend.</title>
<headline>U.N. sources see Iraq aid plan approved by weekend.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Approval by the United Nations Secretary-General of Iraq's aid distribution plan, which has held up the start of the second round of the &quot;oil-for-food&quot; scheme for two months, is expected by this weekend, according to well-placed sources at the U.N.</p>
<p>&quot;We have said that we would approve it by the end of July and I would say give or take a day or so we will have it done,&quot; said a senior U.N. official involved in the review of the deal.  </p>
<p>&quot;There is still an issue about 'vulnerable groups' but it is our understanding that it will be approved over the weekend,&quot; said a Western diplomat.</p>
</text>
